# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# the agent tooling — tooling dev-time (FSL-1.1-MIT), NO forma parte del producto.
# Aisotropy es un producto soberano MIT/Apache-2.0: mantenemos el tooling FSL
# fuera de la historia de git. COS sigue funcionando localmente (los hooks se
# leen del disco); solo no se trackea. Cada dev lo instala con install.sh.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.agent-tooling/
.claude/
agent-tooling.yaml
# Proyecciones del mismo contenido para otros arneses (Codex, agentes genéricos).
# Se generan por find/replace desde .claude/ — p. ej. .codex/hooks/*.sh es
# byte-idéntico a su gemelo en .claude/hooks/, y .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md solo
# cambia "claude-code"→"Codex". Si el canónico no se trackea, la proyección
# tampoco: de lo contrario el repo público publicaría por la puerta de atrás la
# config de agentes que el resto del repo deliberadamente no publica.
.agents/
.codex/

# ── Go (producto) ──
# Binarios compilados y artefactos de build.
/aisotropyd
# Dev-tool binaries dropped by `go build ./cmd/X` without -o (run these via `go run`).
/bitrate-harness
/skill-import
/embed-bench
/bin/
*.exe
*.out
*.test
# Compiled example bots: each example is its own module, so `go build ./...`
# (or `go build .`) drops a binary named after the directory next to its go.mod.
# Those are build artifacts — never commit them. When you add an example, add a
# line here for its binary (one per module; gitignore can't match "extensionless
# file named after its dir" generically).
/examples/weatherbot/weatherbot
/examples/helpdesk/helpdesk
# Stray dev-console binary (go build ./cmd/x → ./x).
/x
# Cobertura
*.cover
coverage.out

# ── Entorno / secretos ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Runtime config FILE (aisotropy/runtimeconfig.go, ADR-0040) — an operator's local,
# environment-specific copy, never a repo artifact. This is the SECOND barrier, not
# the defense: `git add -f` walks straight past .gitignore, so per ADR-0072 the
# loader itself REFUSES to read any secret-bearing key from these files.
# The committed reference `aisotropy.runtime.example.yaml` is deliberately kept
# (negated below) — it carries no secret keys, guarded by
# TestExampleRuntimeConfig_IsRealAndInert.
aisotropy.runtime*.yaml
aisotropy.runtime*.yml
aisotropy.runtime*.toml
!aisotropy.runtime.example.yaml

