# ── Arena runtime state (never commit) ──
arenas/live/*/.aisotropy-data
arenas/live/*/.aisotropy-data.arena-run-marker
arenas/live/*/.data

# Python bytecode (examples/ PoCs)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Compiled footprint/bench binaries. Go bakes ABSOLUTE build paths into the
# binary, so committing one publishes the builder's home directory and real name
# to anyone who runs `strings` on it — and a binary in git history cannot be
# removed without rewriting every commit after it. This repo already carries one
# such blob in history (arenas/adk-go/parity, 21.5 MB, found by the
# pre-publication audit); arenas/.gitignore was added reactively for that case.
# These patterns close the remaining class BEFORE a `git add -A` makes it
# permanent.
bench/footprint/*/adk-go-footprint
bench/footprint/*/*-footprint

# Runner artifacts and local working notes — regenerated or machine-local, and
# the same "untracked but not ignored" trap as the compiled binaries above: a
# single `git add -A` before publication would commit them permanently.
# The durable record stream: the ONLY source from which a board can be
# re-rendered, drift-checked or re-analysed at cell level. Gitignored because it
# is large and regenerated per run — but that also means git cannot recover it,
# and the runner APPENDS to it on every invocation, so a small debugging run
# mixes into a finished board. An Agnes board's 780 records were destroyed this
# way on 2026-07-28 (a failed `head -n -2` whose redirect emptied the file).
# scripts/arena-post-board.sh now archives it read-only as its FIRST action —
# archive the artefact before anything is allowed to touch it.
arenas/live/RESULTS.records.jsonl
# Read-only per-board archives written by arena-post-board.sh. Kept out of git
# for size; they are the local safety net, not the published evidence (RESULTS.md
# is, and it IS committed).
arenas/live/.records-archive/
CACHE.md
